# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) for `wrangler dev`.
#
# There is deliberately no Supabase service-role key here, and there should
# never be one. The server verifies tokens with the project's *public* JWKS, so
# it needs no credential that could be used to mint an identity or read a table.
# If a future feature seems to need the service key, that is the moment to ask
# whether the client should be doing it against Supabase's own row-level
# security instead.

# Your Supabase project URL. Leave empty to run the server with no identity
# provider — /health will say `identityConfigured: false` and sockets will be
# refused, which is the honest behaviour rather than a permissive one.
SUPABASE_URL=""

# Guards two routes, and it is worth knowing both before treating this as a
# development convenience:
#
#   POST /match/:id/init          creates a match, until the matchmaker (§9) owns it
#   GET|PUT /admin/saves/:id/profile   reads and writes ONE named account's profile
#                                      save, for `node scripts/grant.mjs`
#
# The second names an account in the path rather than deriving it from a token,
# so this string is the only thing between a stranger and any player's save.
# Treat it like a password, not like a feature flag. It is never in the client
# bundle, is refused on any request carrying an Origin header, and with this
# left empty both routes are closed entirely.
#
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
ADMIN_TOKEN=""
